Subject: the simulation's seams: a told log, one clock on simulated shards, binds by port, a planted commit
Why: Quiver's persisted class runs in a deterministic simulation (kiln's CP-T2.2 step 6, docs/design/persisted-sim.md). A told log (Waits::Told) writes only when its caller cuts (Log::cut) and reads a waking fetch only when served (Log::serve). Its restore at open, and any caller that waits on its write or fetch, tell it by waiting. Every driver on a simulated shard reads one clock (hyper_rt::sim::anchor, shard_instant). A simulated bind takes the port asked for in its shard. Mutant::OwnLogCommit is the planted bug, through Replica::plant. Offered upstream as hyper-raft's cp/t2.2-told.

